Ever feel sleepy, tired, or craving sugar right after eating?
That’s often a glucose spike.

When you eat refined carbs or sugar, glucose floods into your bloodstream.
Your pancreas releases insulin to control it… but repeated spikes force your body to work overtime.

That’s when the crashes hit — fatigue, brain fog, headaches, low energy.

Over time, constant spikes can lead to insulin resistance and serious health problems.

But small habits change everything.

Eat fiber and protein before carbs.
Avoid sugary drinks.
And take a short walk after meals.

Steadier glucose.
Less stress on your body.
More stable energy.